  "notes": [
    "`commit` pins the upstream SHA for content markdown (`<contentRoot>/<slug>/content/<topic>@<nodeId>.md`). Since the 2026 restructure the repo holds content only; the React Flow layout JSON is fetched live from `<layoutBaseUrl>/<slug>.json` and cached under `.cache/upstream/<commit>/site/` — that cached copy is the reproducibility record, so commit a sync and its cache together in spirit: never regenerate without reviewing remap.log.json.",
    "include[] entries are carried forward from the previous disciplines.generated.json unless flagged `fetchFromUpstream: true` (site layout for `upstreamId ?? id`, or repo file at `upstreamPath` when set; skill ids are preserved against the prior payload by node id → upstream oldId → unique label) or `source: \"custom\"` (hand-authored file at `customPath`). Carried-forward disciplines (html, css, shell-bash, nextjs, docker, django, kotlin, scala, swift-ui, network-engineer, elasticsearch) have site layouts available too but have not been re-derived yet.",
    "`contentSlug` (defaults to `upstreamId ?? id`) names the upstream content folder used to fill empty resource lists and to recover unlinked skills.",
    "Bump `commit`, add/remove entries, then run `pnpm run sync:disciplines && pnpm run data:check`."
  ],
